course: everyday
lesson: 422
title: GTA 6: what rated 18 means
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: At lunch Theo announced: «I'm getting GTA 6 for my birthday.» Within a minute the whole table was talking about it as if they had all played it for years. Jayden said that in GTA 6 you can fly to the Moon in a taxi. Someone else said you can buy a whole city. Kai asked the only sensible question: «If it's so great, why is it rated 18?» Nobody knew. It turned out that Jayden had made up the Moon taxi to impress everyone, and that Theo had asked for it but his mum had already said no. «I said I was GETTING it,» Theo mumbled. «I didn't say I was getting it.»
explain: At home Zara asked her mum what «mature content» on the box meant. Her mum explained that the age rating is not about how hard a game is, it is about what is in it: lots of realistic violence, crime, strong swearing and grown-up scenes. Grown-ups can watch that and know it is a story; for a nine-year-old it can be frightening, or it can make cruelty look normal and funny. «So it's not that I'm too bad at games,» said Zara. «It's that it's not made for your age,» said her mum, «like a horror film isn't.»
explain: Priya only wanted to explore GTA 6's huge sunny world, drive along the beach and look at the sunsets. Her dad said that was fair to want, and found her a different open-world game rated for her age where she can do just that. Ollie's dad plays GTA 6 after Ollie goes to bed, with headphones on. «Why is it OK for Dad?» Ollie asked. «Because I'm forty-one,» said Dad, «and because I can stop and think, that's just a game, I'd never do that.»
explain: Leo's friend said «my parents let me play GTA 6». Leo's mum said: «Different families decide different things, but in this house we follow the rating.» Mia saw GTA 6 in a shop and asked if they check ages. The shop assistant said yes: in the UK it is against the law to sell an 18-rated game to anyone under 18, and she had sent a boy away the day before even though he said it was for his uncle. Noah groaned that waiting until 18 is forever. His big cousin laughed: «There'll be GTA 9 by then, mate.»
fact: In the UK and Europe, games carry a PEGI age rating such as 3, 7, 12, 16 or 18.
fact: A PEGI 7 game may have only mild, cartoon-style fighting, like soft cartoon monsters; PEGI 16 and 18 games have realistic violence.
fact: In the USA and Canada, games carry an ESRB rating; «M» means Mature, for ages 17 and up.
fact: An age rating tells you what is in a game, not how hard the game is to play.
fact: A game rated 18 can contain realistic violence, crime, strong swearing and adult scenes.
fact: In the UK it is against the law for a shop to sell a game rated 12, 16 or 18 to someone younger than that age.
fact: Content made for grown-ups can frighten younger children or make cruelty seem normal and funny.
fact: Many games with big worlds to explore are made for younger players too.
fact: Different families make different choices, but the rating is the official advice for every family.
fact: Stories told at school about what happens in a game are often exaggerated or made up.
fact: A grown-up playing an 18 game is not breaking a rule, because the rating is about the player's age.
exercise: What does an age rating on a game tell you? | What kind of content the game contains | How difficult the levels of the game are | How many hours the game takes to finish | How much the game costs in the shop
exercise: Why is GTA 6 rated 18? | It has realistic violence, crime and strong swearing | It is too hard for anyone under 18 to win | It is the most expensive game in the shop | It needs a grown-up's bank card to start
exercise: Why did the class talk about GTA 6 as if they had played it? | To look cool and grown-up in front of others | Because the school had shown it in an assembly | Because it was free on every console | Because they had read the game's manual
exercise: What was true about Jayden's Moon taxi? | He made it up to impress the class | It is the best secret in the game | It only works on Tuesdays in the game | It needs a special code from the shop
exercise: What had really happened with Theo's birthday present? | His mum had already said no | His mum had already bought it | He had played it at a friend's | He had won it in a competition
exercise: How did Theo probably feel when the truth came out? | Embarrassed, because he had been showing off | Proud, because everyone had believed his story | Angry, because Kai had lied about him | Bored, because he never liked the game
exercise: What did Zara's mum compare GTA 6 to? | A horror film that is not for her age | A maths test that is far too difficult for her | A book with very small writing | A football match for grown-ups
exercise: Why can grown-up content be bad for a nine-year-old? | It can frighten them or make cruelty look normal | It makes children's eyes work less well over time | It teaches them to drive too early | It makes all other games feel too easy
exercise: What did Priya really want from GTA 6? | To explore a big sunny world | To fight with other players | To learn how to steal cars | To beat her dad's high score
exercise: What did Priya's dad do that was wise? | Found her an open-world game rated for her age | Let her play GTA 6 with her eyes closed | Told her never to explore any game world | Bought GTA 6 and kept it on a high shelf for later
exercise: Why is it fine for Ollie's dad to play GTA 6? | He is a grown-up, so the rating fits him | He plays it only with the sound turned off | He plays it on a different console | He promised never to finish the game
exercise: What did Leo's mum say about the friend whose parents allow GTA 6? | Different families decide, but they follow the rating | That family must be breaking the law | Leo should stop being friends with him | Leo can play it at his friend's house
exercise: Why did the shop assistant send the boy away? | Selling an 18 game to a child is against the law | The game had already sold out that morning, so none were left | He did not have enough money for it | The shop only sells games to uncles
exercise: In the USA, which rating would a game like GTA 6 most likely get? | M, for Mature, ages 17 and up | E, for Everyone, all ages | T, for Teen, ages 13 and up | E10+, for ages ten and up
exercise: What did Kai do that was clever at lunch? | He asked why the game was rated 18 | He pretended he had played it too, all weekend | He made up a story about the game | He stayed quiet and ate his lunch
exercise: What kind of courage would it take to say «I haven't played it» at that table? | Being honest when everyone else is showing off | Shouting louder than everybody else | Bringing the game to school the next day | Inventing a better story than Jayden
test: «GTA 6 is rated 18 cos it's dead hard, ur too rubbish for it». True? | No, the rating is about content, not difficulty | Yes, 18 games are much harder than others | Yes, only adults can press the buttons fast | No, it's rated 18 because it's expensive
test: Jayden: «u can fly to the moon in a taxi in GTA, swear down». What's most likely? | He made it up to impress people | It is true, every player has done it | It is true if you play past midnight | It is a secret only Jayden knows
test: Boy in the shop: «it's for my uncle, honest». The assistant still says no. Why? | She can't sell an 18 game to a child | She doesn't believe he has an uncle at all | The game is only for shop workers | The uncle must sign a letter first
test: «my mum lets me play GTA 6 so it's fine for u too». What's the best answer? | My family follows the rating, that's our choice | Then your mum is breaking the law | Fine, I'll tell my mum yours said it's OK | Then I'll play it at yours without asking
test: Ollie: «not fair, Dad plays GTA every night!!» What's the fair reply? | Dad is a grown-up, the rating is about age | Dad is breaking the rules too, tell on him | Ollie can play it when Dad is asleep | It's fair only if Dad plays quietly
test: Zara sees «mature content» on a box. What does that mean? | It has things made for grown-ups only | The game is very old and very well made | The game teaches you to be grown-up | The game is for very good players
test: Priya: «I just want the beach and the sunsets tho». What's the best plan? | Find a big-world game rated for her age | Play GTA 6 but only ever look at the sunsets | Wait until her parents are out | Watch the scary bits with eyes shut
test: Noah: «waiting till 18 is literally forever». What's true? | There are loads of great games for his age now | He will never be allowed any games before 18 | Games will stop being made before then | He can ask the shop to change the rating
test: Which rating is most likely on a game where kids build with blocks and fight soft cartoon zombies? | PEGI 7 | PEGI 18 | PEGI 16 | PEGI 12
test: Theo: «I said I was GETTING it, I didn't say I was getting it». What was Theo doing at lunch? | Showing off with a half-truth | Telling the whole truth clearly | Talking about a different game | Explaining what the rating means
test: Teacher: «Who has actually played GTA 6?» Nobody puts a hand up. What does this show? | The lunch stories were mostly made up | Everyone was too shy to put their hand up | The teacher asked the wrong question | GTA 6 is played only at night
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the information conveyed by an age rating? | It indicates the nature of the content contained therein | It indicates the degree of difficulty of the game | It indicates the duration required for completion | It indicates the recommended retail price
exam: It is given that a retailer in the United Kingdom is requested to supply a game rated 18 to a minor. Select the response consistent with the established facts. | The sale is prohibited by law and must be refused | The sale is permitted if the minor so requests | The sale is permitted for the benefit of a relative | The sale is permitted on the minor's birthday
exam: Identify the principal reason for which content intended for adults is deemed unsuitable for a child of nine years. | It may frighten the child or normalise cruelty | It may impair the functioning of the child's eyes | It may render the child unable to play other games | It may cause the console to function improperly
exam: Determine which of the following constitutes the designation applied in the United States to a game suitable for persons aged seventeen and above. | M, signifying Mature | E, signifying Everyone | T, signifying Teen | E10+, signifying ten and above
